 Determination of visual percentage and optical properties of asbestos and non-asbestos material;
 Must be able to see accurately sight colors through microscope;
 Submits all QC data reports as directed;
 Establishes or adjusts workflow to meet turnaround time schedules;
 Operate an autoclave;
 Ensure that company polices are adhered to;
 Ensure that work-scheduled procedures adequately address client needs;
 Provide customer service to clients;
 Other laboratory duties as assigned.
The candidate must be fully trained and proficient in performing PLM bulk asbestos analysis as part of the role.
 University degree or college diploma in a science field.
 Basic computer literacy;
 Laboratory safety and WHMIS training;
 Technical knowledge of applicable test methods
 Monday to Friday: 7:30am to 4pm (potential weekend/evening work as required).
